# Git remotes

This repo has two remotes:

- `origin` (`thom-at-redhat/configiq`) — the primary repo for this project.
  It has its own CI and Vercel deployment. All branches, PRs, and MRs are
  pushed here.
- `upstream` (`openshift-psap/configiq`) — reference-only. Fetch from it if
  you need to compare or pull in changes, but never push to it.

## Rule

**Never open a PR or MR against `upstream`.** Even though this project
started as a fork, `upstream` is not the collaboration target — all pull
requests / merge requests target `origin/main`.

- When using `gh pr create` (or any MR tooling), always verify the target
  repo/base resolves to `origin`, not `upstream`.
- Do not push branches to `upstream` under any circumstances.
